# std.function: the function type constructors and the `Tuple` marker trait
# (spec/lang/07-functions.md#function-type-constructors).
#
# `Fn` and `SuspendFn` are the constructors that `fn(...) -> O $ R` and
# `fn!(...) -> O $ R` stand for. They have no fields and no construction
# syntax, so the compiler rewrites a spelled one to its sugar
# (src/checker/function-types.ts) and they need no declaration here.

# An empty sealed marker trait that every tuple type implements: `()`,
# `(A,)`, and a tuple with a rest element included
# (r-fn.type.ctor.tuple-trait, r-fn.type.ctor.tuple-trait.rest). Only the
# compiler implements it, as it does `Inspectable` (r-trait.sealed.tuple).
pub trait Tuple
